% R11: Every accepted order can be prepared and loaded during normal operation, without requiring an emergency.
% Scope: six belt positions, two tables, three total orders; atomic events.
% Capability: a successful path exists; this does not promise service on every execution.

% CHECK: load-capability
% AcceptOrder hides its ID; nextID counts acceptances from zero. The diamond asks for one normal preparation/loading path.
(
nu Orders(nextID: OrderID = 0) .
(
    forall meal: Meal, tbl: TableID . [AcceptOrder(meal, tbl)]
    (
        <(!StartEmergency)* . AddPlate(nextID, tbl) .
         (!StartEmergency)* . (LoadPlate(nextID) | PlateLoaded(plate(nextID, tbl)))> true
        && Orders(nextID + 1)
    )
    && [!(exists meal: Meal, tbl: TableID . AcceptOrder(meal, tbl))] Orders(nextID)
)
)
% END CHECK
